deadline: "2026-08-14T20:21:27.042Z"
assignee: codex-root
author: codex-root
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: "Built hassio provides bounded entity-delta watching with entity/domain filters, max-event and duration limits, deterministic normalized output, and explicit unsubscribe cleanup; Built hassio provides bounded trigger and condition platform discovery using current Home Assistant subscription contracts; All output formats and schema/help surfaces document stable programmatic envelopes; All source tests retain exact 100/100/100/100 coverage and repository quality/release gates pass; Live Home Assistant 2026.7.4 read-only acceptance succeeds without persisting private payloads"
definition_of_ready: "Official docs, tagged Core 2026.7.4 source, live instance version, all-status PM lineage, GitHub issues/PRs, installed dependency types, and release failure logs inspected"
goal: agent-native-home-state-observation
objective: typed-bounded-websocket-deltas-and-platforms
value: Let agents observe only meaningful state changes and discover automation primitives without polling full state snapshots or parsing raw protocol envelopes.
impact: Reduces token and bandwidth cost while making current Home Assistant automation capabilities directly usable in safe programmatic workflows.
outcome: "A typed, documented, production-ready live observation and automation discovery surface with exact release evidence."
why_now: Home Assistant 2026.7 promotes purpose-specific automations and its current Core protocol offers delta subscriptions not yet modeled by the CLI.
